1
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:08,279
ATSUSHI MATSUYAMA - CUSTOMS OFFICER

2
00:00:08,363 --> 00:00:10,073
Even if you keep nagging me like that…

3
00:00:10,156 --> 00:00:12,116
It's not that I don't want to do it.

4
00:00:13,785 --> 00:00:16,329
Come on, don't say that.
You're threatening me…

5
00:00:19,707 --> 00:00:23,086
I'll call you back later
to discuss this. Bye.

6
00:00:24,379 --> 00:00:25,380
Where did you come from?

7
00:00:25,463 --> 00:00:27,632
The next flight will be arriving shortly.

8
00:00:27,715 --> 00:00:30,009
Today, children on a field trip
are coming,

9
00:00:30,093 --> 00:00:31,761
so we were told to do a thorough job.

10
00:00:31,845 --> 00:00:34,055
I always do a thorough job.

11
00:01:00,415 --> 00:01:01,249
He's getting grilled.

12
00:01:01,833 --> 00:01:04,586
I wouldn't be able to take that.

13
00:01:04,669 --> 00:01:05,962
You will inspect them,

14
00:01:06,045 --> 00:01:08,214
every single one of them.
These are important to me.

15
00:01:08,298 --> 00:01:11,426
This is Customs. What Customs does.

16
00:01:11,509 --> 00:01:13,720
-is finding things that must not
-You all have things

17
00:01:13,803 --> 00:01:15,597
-be brought into Japan.
-you keep by your side, right?

18
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:16,556
-Where?
-Fine.

19
00:01:17,640 --> 00:01:19,184
Why are you coming now?

20
00:01:19,267 --> 00:01:20,685
I didn't mean to!

21
00:01:21,978 --> 00:01:24,355
What is he doing?

22
00:01:24,439 --> 00:01:25,440
Are you getting scolded?

23
00:01:25,523 --> 00:01:27,734
-Do what you want!
-I am not getting scolded.

24
00:01:27,817 --> 00:01:28,776
You look kind of lame.

25
00:01:28,860 --> 00:01:31,738
Not all adult jobs are cool.

26
00:01:31,821 --> 00:01:33,364
‎Fine, fine. Go ahead!

27
00:01:33,448 --> 00:01:35,199
Um…

28
00:01:35,283 --> 00:01:38,912
He's fighting so that he can conduct
an important inspection…

29
00:01:39,746 --> 00:01:41,623
-…for us.
-He's fighting?

30
00:01:41,706 --> 00:01:43,458
-Yes.
-God, What a day!

31
00:01:43,541 --> 00:01:46,294
-You got this!
-I had a bad feeling about today.

32
00:01:46,377 --> 00:01:49,130
-You got this!
-You got this!

33
00:01:49,214 --> 00:01:53,259
From the moment I woke up,
I had a bad feeling about today!

34
00:01:53,885 --> 00:01:55,094
You got this!

35
00:01:55,178 --> 00:01:56,596
This is chaos.

36
00:01:56,679 --> 00:01:58,640
-You got this!
-You got this!

37
00:01:58,723 --> 00:02:01,976
-You got this!
-You got this!

38
00:02:06,731 --> 00:02:08,733
You and I spent two hours

39
00:02:08,816 --> 00:02:11,361
checking the contents
of 42 USB flash drives.

40
00:02:11,444 --> 00:02:13,655
I'm completely exhausted.

41
00:02:13,738 --> 00:02:15,740
So, did anything come up?

42
00:02:15,823 --> 00:02:17,367
Yes, something did.

43
00:02:17,450 --> 00:02:19,577
Videos and photos he took
of his three growing children.

44
00:02:19,661 --> 00:02:21,287
Family photos?

45
00:02:21,371 --> 00:02:23,539
During the clip of his
daughter's piano recital,

46
00:02:23,623 --> 00:02:26,209
that huge guy watched it
with us and was tearing up.

47
00:02:26,876 --> 00:02:28,336
It was a waste of effort.

48
00:02:28,419 --> 00:02:33,007
But sometimes people smuggle in data
hidden in those videos. It's quite common.

49
00:02:33,091 --> 00:02:35,385
Yes. Yes!

50
00:02:35,468 --> 00:02:38,054
What do they call them again…

51
00:02:38,137 --> 00:02:40,515
-Cold wallets?
-Cold wallets, yes, that's it!

52
00:02:40,598 --> 00:02:42,767
The thing they use to hide crypto profits
to dodge taxes.

53
00:02:42,850 --> 00:02:43,810
It's important work.

54
00:02:43,893 --> 00:02:45,895
Because Immigration
won't do it themselves.

55
00:02:45,979 --> 00:02:49,983
Our work isn't manual labor.
It's to, you know…

56
00:02:50,066 --> 00:02:52,151
-Mental labor.
-It's mental labor.

57
00:02:55,947 --> 00:02:58,199
-Is that all?
-Yes.

58
00:03:00,284 --> 00:03:02,161
Are you feeling okay?

59
00:03:39,615 --> 00:03:41,034
Shibuya Scramble Crossing.

60
00:03:41,117 --> 00:03:45,246
And, and, and ramen!
I really, really have to try it.

61
00:03:45,330 --> 00:03:46,748
I'm glad to hear that.

62
00:03:46,831 --> 00:03:49,751
However, it's best
not to make jokes like that.

63
00:03:49,834 --> 00:03:51,836
Sometimes they aren't
taken as jokes. Go ahead.

64
00:03:52,795 --> 00:03:53,755
Sorry.

65
00:03:53,838 --> 00:03:57,884
Is this all of your luggage?
Please let me inspect it.

66
00:04:01,054 --> 00:04:02,305
Thank you.

67
00:04:02,388 --> 00:04:05,433
He's so by the book.
He can't even take a joke.

68
00:04:06,142 --> 00:04:08,895
I agree, he's a hardass.

69
00:04:08,978 --> 00:04:12,148
However, we are not here to have
casual conversation with customers.

70
00:04:12,231 --> 00:04:13,733
I know. It's just that

71
00:04:13,816 --> 00:04:17,945
coming to Japan has been
my dream for so long.

72
00:04:18,029 --> 00:04:22,200
But, yeah, I guess
I got a little bit carried away.

73
00:04:23,368 --> 00:04:24,869
-Go ahead.
-Thank you.

74
00:04:25,703 --> 00:04:27,789
-Excuse me. Could I see one more thing?
-Huh?

75
00:04:28,498 --> 00:04:31,501
-May I see that necklace?
-Oh, yes.

76
00:04:32,085 --> 00:04:34,462
-Here you go.
-Thank you very much.

77
00:04:37,423 --> 00:04:40,676
-This is soil inside, right?
-Yes.

78
00:04:41,594 --> 00:04:44,722
I'm sorry, but it will
have to be confiscated.

79
00:04:45,306 --> 00:04:46,224
Confiscated?

80
00:04:46,808 --> 00:04:49,477
You cannot bring
foreign soil into the country.

81
00:04:50,103 --> 00:04:52,313
What? Even just a tiny amount?

82
00:04:52,397 --> 00:04:54,899
It's prohibited, regardless of the amount.

83
00:04:56,109 --> 00:04:57,777
I really like it.

84
00:04:58,486 --> 00:05:01,197
I'm sorry, I'm quite by the book myself.

85
00:05:02,990 --> 00:05:05,243
-It's okay. I get it.
-Thank you very much.

86
00:05:06,452 --> 00:05:08,371
Plant Protection, please.

87
00:05:11,541 --> 00:05:12,667
Is this okay?

88
00:05:14,293 --> 00:05:16,587
Yes. Thank you very much.

89
00:05:18,089 --> 00:05:20,925
-Am I free to go now?
-Of course.

90
00:05:21,968 --> 00:05:24,554
Which means I'm free to go as well.

91
00:05:25,721 --> 00:05:28,349
-Just this way, please.
-Okay.

92
00:05:28,433 --> 00:05:30,518
Hayami, do you cook?

93
00:05:31,310 --> 00:05:32,895
Yes, I do.

94
00:05:32,979 --> 00:05:34,939
Really? What can you make?

95
00:05:36,315 --> 00:05:38,818
-Pasta and stuff.
-Pasta? Wow…

96
00:05:38,901 --> 00:05:40,236
-I'll be leaving now.
-See you.

97
00:05:40,319 --> 00:05:41,320
Are you leaving already?

98
00:05:42,029 --> 00:05:44,323
I was thinking of getting dinner
since my wife isn't home.

99
00:05:44,407 --> 00:05:45,283
Care to join me?

100
00:05:45,992 --> 00:05:47,285
I'm sorry. Not today.

101
00:05:48,161 --> 00:05:49,620
-I see.
-Goodbye.

102
00:05:49,704 --> 00:05:51,289
Bye.

103
00:05:51,998 --> 00:05:54,125
Pasta is nice…

104
00:05:54,208 --> 00:05:56,419
What kinds of pasta are you good at?

105
00:05:56,502 --> 00:06:00,173
-Well, I guess Roman pasta…
-Roman pasta!? That's…

106
00:06:00,756 --> 00:06:01,674
Hayami, is that…

107
00:06:03,467 --> 00:06:06,429
No wonder he turned down my invitation.

108
00:06:07,889 --> 00:06:09,182
By the way, Hayami,

109
00:06:09,265 --> 00:06:11,100
-I'd like to try your--
-I'm sorry.

110
00:06:11,184 --> 00:06:12,393
I'm also busy today.

111
00:06:15,938 --> 00:06:16,939
I see.

112
00:06:23,196 --> 00:06:26,616
-Good morning.
-Morning.

113
00:06:29,327 --> 00:06:30,578
What's happening?

114
00:06:32,288 --> 00:06:34,457
Everyone's here.

115
00:06:35,833 --> 00:06:38,628
This is Nishida
from the Metropolitan Police Department.

116
00:06:38,711 --> 00:06:40,421
I'm Nishida from the First Division.

117
00:06:40,504 --> 00:06:44,175
He's here to ask about the murder case
that occurred last night.

118
00:06:44,258 --> 00:06:45,509
Murder case?

119
00:06:45,593 --> 00:06:48,846
The name of the murdered victim
is Amita Barad.

120
00:06:48,930 --> 00:06:50,181
She was a female university student

121
00:06:50,264 --> 00:06:52,892
-who arrived from the Republic of Chatwan.
-Amita Barad…

122
00:06:52,975 --> 00:06:53,976
Her!

123
00:06:58,147 --> 00:07:01,776
Given the short time between the victim's
entry into the country and the incident,

124
00:07:01,859 --> 00:07:04,654
it's possible the perpetrator
followed her from the airport.

125
00:07:05,404 --> 00:07:06,739
I'd like to ask about her entry.

126
00:07:06,822 --> 00:07:10,034
Of course, we won't hesitate
to cooperate with the police.

127
00:07:10,117 --> 00:07:11,202
Thank you very much.

128
00:07:12,286 --> 00:07:13,538
Well then, you.

129
00:07:14,580 --> 00:07:16,040
What, me?

130
00:07:16,123 --> 00:07:18,960
Actually, this was found
on the victim's smartphone.

131
00:07:27,301 --> 00:07:28,636
‎Oh my…

132
00:07:30,471 --> 00:07:32,557
You and the victim
had never met before that point.

133
00:07:33,891 --> 00:07:35,268
Is that correct?

134
00:07:36,644 --> 00:07:37,645
Yes.

135
00:07:38,980 --> 00:07:42,775
And yet, the victim had a picture of you.

136
00:07:42,858 --> 00:07:43,943
Why is that?

137
00:07:44,485 --> 00:07:45,361
Well…

138
00:07:46,153 --> 00:07:48,614
I don't know. I have no idea.

139
00:07:49,115 --> 00:07:50,408
I see…

140
00:07:52,827 --> 00:07:54,453
But isn't that strange?

141
00:07:57,123 --> 00:08:00,835
"The body found in a park in Suginami Ward
in the early hours of the morning

142
00:08:00,918 --> 00:08:02,420
was identified as 25-year-old Amita Barad,

143
00:08:02,503 --> 00:08:04,630
a traveler from the Republic of Chatwan."

144
00:08:04,714 --> 00:08:07,466
To think this would happen
to that woman who entered yesterday.

145
00:08:07,550 --> 00:08:11,429
Suginami Ward isn't an unsafe area either.

146
00:08:11,512 --> 00:08:13,848
Still, it's not really
a place tourists go to.

147
00:08:13,931 --> 00:08:15,850
Maybe she had an acquaintance there.

148
00:08:15,933 --> 00:08:18,311
She didn't seem like she was going
to meet an acquaintance, though.

149
00:08:19,395 --> 00:08:22,356
-Why is that?
-She was eager to do sightseeing.

150
00:08:22,982 --> 00:08:25,651
But she also said something alarming.

151
00:08:28,237 --> 00:08:31,741
She joked that she came here
to smuggle drugs.

152
00:08:32,325 --> 00:08:33,367
Smuggle?

153
00:08:42,835 --> 00:08:45,004
-How did it go?
-What did he ask you?

154
00:08:45,087 --> 00:08:46,797
Nothing much, really.

155
00:08:46,881 --> 00:08:48,883
She's the girl
you were with yesterday, right?

156
00:08:49,925 --> 00:08:52,345
-Yes.
-What's with her having a photo

157
00:08:52,428 --> 00:08:54,430
-of you on her phone?
-Well…

158
00:08:55,097 --> 00:08:57,391
How should I know?

159
00:08:57,475 --> 00:08:59,268
I'm going to the inspection booth.

160
00:08:59,352 --> 00:09:00,269
Okay.

161
00:09:05,274 --> 00:09:09,362
It must be a shock, having someone
you inspected end up like that.

162
00:09:10,738 --> 00:09:14,116
Do you think what she said
was really just a joke?

163
00:09:22,958 --> 00:09:27,880
DO NOT ENTER

164
00:09:40,935 --> 00:09:43,521
-Was Matsuyama really called in again?
-Yes.

165
00:09:43,604 --> 00:09:47,108
They want to double-check something with
Matsuyama since he inspected her luggage.

166
00:09:47,191 --> 00:09:48,401
But why?

167
00:09:48,484 --> 00:09:51,195
-This time, those two came as well.
-Those two?

168
00:09:51,278 --> 00:09:53,447
Inspector Iuchi
and Assistant Inspector Nakatsuka.

169
00:09:53,531 --> 00:09:55,241
Those two aren't from the First Division.

170
00:09:55,324 --> 00:09:57,284
They are from
the International Crime Division.

171
00:09:57,368 --> 00:09:58,494
-Right?
-Yes.

172
00:09:58,577 --> 00:10:02,498
The First Investigation Division
and the International Crime Division…

173
00:10:05,292 --> 00:10:06,836
It's strange.

174
00:10:06,919 --> 00:10:09,839
You take the train when commuting
to and from here, don't you?

175
00:10:09,922 --> 00:10:14,051
But the station is in the opposite
direction from that bus stop.

176
00:10:14,969 --> 00:10:17,430
Why did you go over there?

177
00:10:17,513 --> 00:10:21,934
I had plans to meet an acquaintance
that day, so I didn't take the train.

178
00:10:22,893 --> 00:10:26,939
So, on that day of all days, you didn't
use the train, walked to the bus stop,

179
00:10:27,022 --> 00:10:28,691
and happened to run into her.

180
00:10:30,526 --> 00:10:32,486
That's a remarkably convenient story.

181
00:10:32,570 --> 00:10:35,406
That happens to be the truth,
so what choice do I have?

182
00:10:35,489 --> 00:10:36,866
What exactly are you trying to say?

183
00:10:38,492 --> 00:10:41,996
You knew the victim beforehand,
didn't you?

184
00:10:47,626 --> 00:10:50,045
I have nothing more to say to you.

185
00:10:50,129 --> 00:10:51,213
Excuse me.

186
00:10:55,301 --> 00:10:57,094
We're not finished talking.

187
00:10:58,721 --> 00:11:00,139
Sit down.

188
00:11:04,435 --> 00:11:07,605
Why do we have to wait
in a place like this?

189
00:11:07,688 --> 00:11:10,316
What choice do we have? He always
wants to do everything by himself.

190
00:11:10,399 --> 00:11:12,401
Are we just sidekicks?

191
00:11:13,110 --> 00:11:15,488
Is Division One really that special?

192
00:11:23,037 --> 00:11:24,163
What is it?

193
00:11:24,705 --> 00:11:27,416
Why are you interrogating
Matsuyama multiple times?

194
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:29,251
It's not an interrogation.
We're just talking.

195
00:11:29,335 --> 00:11:30,669
Isn't that the same thing?

196
00:11:30,753 --> 00:11:33,797
No, we can't disclose
investigation details.

197
00:11:33,881 --> 00:11:37,176
Now, now, don't be so rigid.
We're practically friends, detectives.

198
00:11:37,259 --> 00:11:39,345
I don't recall becoming friends with you.

199
00:11:40,054 --> 00:11:41,847
Then how about we become friends now?

200
00:11:44,725 --> 00:11:45,601
‎What?

201
00:11:46,727 --> 00:11:47,895
Wait…

202
00:11:47,978 --> 00:11:50,731
-You hear what she's saying?
-Idiot.

203
00:11:58,781 --> 00:11:59,615
Scary.

204
00:11:59,698 --> 00:12:03,744
The two detectives said that if
Matsuyama and Amita knew each other,

205
00:12:03,827 --> 00:12:05,955
they wanted to know the reason why.

206
00:12:06,038 --> 00:12:07,289
What do you mean?

207
00:12:08,749 --> 00:12:10,751
This is strange.

208
00:12:11,919 --> 00:12:12,920
What is this?

209
00:12:13,003 --> 00:12:15,506
This is the footage
from Amita's immigration inspection.

210
00:12:17,383 --> 00:12:20,886
GATE 24 - IN FRONT OF BOOTH A &amp; B

211
00:12:20,970 --> 00:12:22,555
What about it?

212
00:12:22,638 --> 00:12:24,765
Neither booth had a line,

213
00:12:24,848 --> 00:12:27,309
yet she hesitated about
which one to go to.

214
00:12:27,393 --> 00:12:28,602
Now that you mention it…

215
00:12:28,686 --> 00:12:31,522
After that, she looked up
something on her smartphone.

216
00:12:31,605 --> 00:12:34,149
Ah, she's comparing the photo
on her phone with Matsuyama.

217
00:12:34,733 --> 00:12:38,487
Is it possible she chose Matsuyama
specifically to undergo inspection?

218
00:12:38,571 --> 00:12:40,322
She chose Matsuyama? What does that mean?

219
00:12:40,406 --> 00:12:42,116
I don't know.

220
00:12:42,199 --> 00:12:45,119
Well, from the police's perspective,

221
00:12:45,202 --> 00:12:49,123
it looks like she thought
Matsuyama would turn a blind eye

222
00:12:49,206 --> 00:12:51,375
to whatever she was carrying in, right?

223
00:12:52,209 --> 00:12:53,961
Does that mean…

224
00:12:54,044 --> 00:12:55,754
Smuggling?

225
00:12:57,089 --> 00:13:00,426
But Matsuyama confiscated
her necklace, didn't he?

226
00:13:00,509 --> 00:13:02,094
Yes, however…

227
00:13:02,177 --> 00:13:03,178
However?

228
00:13:03,262 --> 00:13:04,930
However,

229
00:13:05,014 --> 00:13:08,642
it could have been a camouflage
to let something else pass through.

230
00:13:08,726 --> 00:13:10,978
That is likely what
the police are suspicious of.

231
00:13:11,061 --> 00:13:14,857
Amita brought something in
with Matsuyama's assistance.

232
00:13:14,940 --> 00:13:17,735
Which led to her being killed.

233
00:13:18,319 --> 00:13:19,778
Is that what you mean?

234
00:13:20,362 --> 00:13:23,907
When viewed that way, it explains why
the First Investigation Division

235
00:13:23,991 --> 00:13:25,951
and International Crime Division
are taking action.

236
00:13:26,869 --> 00:13:28,412
-Um…
-Hm?

237
00:13:29,079 --> 00:13:30,331
Ah, never mind.

238
00:13:30,914 --> 00:13:32,333
Do speak up. Anything is fine.

239
00:13:35,961 --> 00:13:38,797
I saw something.

240
00:13:58,942 --> 00:14:02,571
Come to think of it, he hasn't
been very sociable lately.

241
00:14:03,113 --> 00:14:04,281
He turned down my invitation too…

242
00:14:04,365 --> 00:14:05,824
I don't think that has
anything to do with this.

243
00:14:05,908 --> 00:14:07,951
Ouch, that hit right where it hurts.

244
00:14:08,494 --> 00:14:09,745
Still,

245
00:14:09,828 --> 00:14:13,666
isn't it premature to assume
Matsuyama committed misconduct?

246
00:14:13,749 --> 00:14:15,167
Even though he was given money?

247
00:14:15,250 --> 00:14:19,171
As a bribery case, it's picture-perfect.

248
00:14:20,798 --> 00:14:22,383
What do you think, Mori?

249
00:14:28,931 --> 00:14:30,099
I can't say for sure

250
00:14:30,891 --> 00:14:32,101
without physical evidence.

251
00:14:37,481 --> 00:14:38,857
It's from Matsuyama.

252
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:42,528
He says he's heading straight home
due to feeling unwell.

253
00:14:43,278 --> 00:14:46,198
Being interrogated repeatedly
would do that to anyone.

254
00:14:49,326 --> 00:14:51,245
He's off duty tomorrow, right?

255
00:15:05,175 --> 00:15:07,344
I'm sorry for dragging you
into this on your day off.

256
00:15:07,428 --> 00:15:10,889
No, not at all. I tagged along on my own.

257
00:15:10,973 --> 00:15:13,392
Tailing someone is too heavy
a task for Machi.

258
00:15:13,475 --> 00:15:16,854
Honestly, it could just be me and you.

259
00:15:16,937 --> 00:15:18,772
I've never tailed anyone before.

260
00:15:18,856 --> 00:15:20,357
Me neither.

261
00:15:20,441 --> 00:15:21,442
But

262
00:15:21,525 --> 00:15:25,154
you said you didn't want to leave
questions unanswered, right?

263
00:15:25,738 --> 00:15:26,780
Yes.

264
00:15:26,864 --> 00:15:28,490
Then we have no choice but to investigate.

265
00:15:28,574 --> 00:15:31,410
But would someone suspected
of being an accomplice to smuggling

266
00:15:31,493 --> 00:15:34,329
meet with a member
of a smuggling ring in broad daylight?

267
00:15:36,707 --> 00:15:37,958
Thanks for waiting.

268
00:15:38,459 --> 00:15:41,545
-You can sit over there.
-I'm meeting with him here.

269
00:15:45,090 --> 00:15:48,093
Wait, wait! What are you doing?

270
00:15:48,177 --> 00:15:49,136
Come here.

271
00:15:52,056 --> 00:15:54,391
-I'm going to talk to him.
-What?

272
00:15:54,475 --> 00:15:57,061
We just need to hear
the truth directly from him.

273
00:15:57,144 --> 00:15:59,980
He looks dangerous! What if
something happens to you?

274
00:16:04,193 --> 00:16:05,694
You can let go of me now.

275
00:16:06,528 --> 00:16:08,655
-No.
-What?

276
00:16:11,742 --> 00:16:12,701
Hey.

277
00:16:22,503 --> 00:16:24,797
-Matsuyama.
-Yes?

278
00:16:32,971 --> 00:16:35,182
Who is this man?

279
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:38,227
Were you following me?

280
00:16:38,852 --> 00:16:40,270
That's quite malicious of you.

281
00:16:40,896 --> 00:16:44,983
Endo saw you
receiving money from this man.

282
00:16:45,526 --> 00:16:48,529
So that gives you
the right to snoop around?

283
00:16:48,612 --> 00:16:50,280
No, Matsuyama,

284
00:16:50,364 --> 00:16:52,157
we just want to know the truth.

285
00:16:52,241 --> 00:16:53,700
The truth?

286
00:16:54,910 --> 00:16:58,831
That I took money from this man
and overlooked smuggling?

287
00:16:59,915 --> 00:17:00,749
Did you?

288
00:17:02,209 --> 00:17:03,919
This man is…

289
00:17:05,129 --> 00:17:07,589
Um, the detectives are here again.

290
00:17:07,673 --> 00:17:09,675
-What do you want now?
-I obtained authorization.

291
00:17:11,051 --> 00:17:13,554
I checked your travel history.

292
00:17:13,637 --> 00:17:16,598
You visited Chatwan, the victim's
homeland, last year, didn't you?

293
00:17:17,808 --> 00:17:20,561
Maybe you met her over there?

294
00:17:22,354 --> 00:17:24,148
Why don't you let us hear the details?

295
00:17:27,568 --> 00:17:28,861
Cut it out.

296
00:17:32,072 --> 00:17:33,782
‎Ow, ow, ow…

297
00:17:37,494 --> 00:17:38,954
Obstruction of official duties.

298
00:17:42,082 --> 00:17:43,709
An airport customs officer

299
00:17:43,792 --> 00:17:46,378
was arrested under suspicion
of being an accomplice to smuggling.

300
00:17:46,461 --> 00:17:47,629
This is unprecedented.

301
00:17:47,713 --> 00:17:48,964
COUNSELOR OF BORDER CONTROL REFORM
MIDORI SUGIHARA

302
00:17:49,047 --> 00:17:52,134
Why does Gate 24 keep
bringing one trouble after another?

303
00:17:52,217 --> 00:17:54,303
He hasn't been arrested.

304
00:17:54,386 --> 00:17:55,804
He was merely taken in for questioning.

305
00:17:55,888 --> 00:17:57,389
He was handcuffed, wasn't he?

306
00:17:57,472 --> 00:18:00,350
That was the detective acting out of line.

307
00:18:00,934 --> 00:18:02,853
Matsuyama has already been released.

308
00:18:02,936 --> 00:18:07,357
The smartphone photo,
security camera footage, travel history…

309
00:18:07,441 --> 00:18:09,735
With this much circumstantial evidence
lined up,

310
00:18:09,818 --> 00:18:11,653
an arrest is only a matter of time.

311
00:18:13,071 --> 00:18:14,615
Counselor,

312
00:18:14,698 --> 00:18:17,451
you should take action
before this escalates further.

313
00:18:17,534 --> 00:18:20,954
However, there is also the principle

314
00:18:21,038 --> 00:18:22,998
-of innocent until proven guilty.
-How naive.

315
00:18:23,081 --> 00:18:24,666
An error in judgment

316
00:18:24,750 --> 00:18:27,502
could become an issue
concerning the survival of Gate 24.

317
00:18:28,170 --> 00:18:31,924
Acknowledging that there was
an offender within the team

318
00:18:32,007 --> 00:18:35,093
you personally created must be painful,

319
00:18:35,177 --> 00:18:37,304
but shouldn't you make
a wise decision here?

320
00:18:47,731 --> 00:18:49,900
U-u-um…

321
00:18:51,193 --> 00:18:52,945
We were worried.

322
00:18:53,445 --> 00:18:54,613
Are you all right?

323
00:18:55,656 --> 00:18:56,740
Yes.

324
00:19:01,370 --> 00:19:04,539
This man
is a high school classmate of mine.

325
00:19:05,165 --> 00:19:06,458
A classmate?

326
00:19:07,042 --> 00:19:08,961
-Oh my…
-That rough-looking guy?

327
00:19:09,044 --> 00:19:11,964
Even if he looks rough,
he's far more successful than me.

328
00:19:12,047 --> 00:19:14,258
He started a venture business
right out of high school,

329
00:19:14,341 --> 00:19:16,468
and now he's a CEO
with annual revenue of a billion yen.

330
00:19:16,551 --> 00:19:18,136
Annual revenue of a billion yen?

331
00:19:18,220 --> 00:19:19,054
CEO…

332
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:21,306
Then what I saw was…

333
00:19:22,057 --> 00:19:26,561
It was probably him trying to pay me back
for a meal I paid for him previously.

334
00:19:26,645 --> 00:19:28,605
Hey, that's too much.

335
00:19:28,689 --> 00:19:30,482
Huh? Oh…

336
00:19:30,565 --> 00:19:33,110
I turned it down,
but he forced it into my hand.

337
00:19:33,193 --> 00:19:35,195
But you were handed a stack of bills.

338
00:19:35,279 --> 00:19:38,156
A stack of bills?
It was 20,000 yen at most.

339
00:19:38,240 --> 00:19:40,284
-Here.
-Ah, thank you.

340
00:19:40,367 --> 00:19:43,328
-It wasn't a stack of bills!
-I'm sorry!

341
00:19:43,412 --> 00:19:44,663
He's a genuinely good guy,

342
00:19:44,746 --> 00:19:48,417
and he keeps inviting me to work with him.

343
00:19:49,001 --> 00:19:51,169
-Work together with him?
-And quitting this job?

344
00:19:51,253 --> 00:19:52,337
Why?

345
00:19:52,421 --> 00:19:54,339
You've been working so hard.

346
00:19:54,423 --> 00:19:55,340
Are you dissatisfied here?

347
00:19:55,424 --> 00:19:57,301
You used to grumble that
non-career staff can't move up,

348
00:19:57,384 --> 00:19:59,845
-but that's not the case anymore.
-It's not about that.

349
00:20:02,431 --> 00:20:05,392
You're fluent in English
and good with people,

350
00:20:06,101 --> 00:20:08,186
so you're perfect
for doing sales overseas.

351
00:20:09,062 --> 00:20:12,107
But I like the airport,

352
00:20:12,190 --> 00:20:13,775
and I like this job.

353
00:20:14,901 --> 00:20:16,945
You like it?

354
00:20:18,572 --> 00:20:21,950
Your job is opening people's luggage
and taking away bad stuff, right?

355
00:20:22,993 --> 00:20:24,661
With everyone angry at you.

356
00:20:27,122 --> 00:20:28,707
Angry at me, huh…

357
00:20:29,875 --> 00:20:33,170
Is that a job only you can do?

358
00:20:34,379 --> 00:20:37,466
Let's do something together
that only you can do.

359
00:20:43,430 --> 00:20:45,140
I thought about it.

360
00:20:45,974 --> 00:20:49,144
The suitcases of people on those planes

361
00:20:49,227 --> 00:20:51,229
are stuffed with dreams.

362
00:20:53,273 --> 00:20:54,524
She was like that too.

363
00:20:56,193 --> 00:20:59,196
-Oh, Mr. By-the-Book.
-Hello.

364
00:20:59,279 --> 00:21:02,866
Is this a coincidence, or did you come
to give me back my necklace?

365
00:21:02,949 --> 00:21:04,743
Unfortunately, it's a coincidence.

366
00:21:04,826 --> 00:21:05,994
Aw, too bad.

367
00:21:07,871 --> 00:21:08,997
That reminds me.

368
00:21:09,081 --> 00:21:11,166
I went to your country
as a tourist last year.

369
00:21:11,249 --> 00:21:12,209
It was a wonderful country.

370
00:21:12,292 --> 00:21:13,960
-Really?
-Yes.

371
00:21:14,544 --> 00:21:16,797
But Japan is a wonderful country as well.

372
00:21:16,880 --> 00:21:18,715
Yes, that's true.

373
00:21:18,799 --> 00:21:20,384
I'm only here for a week,

374
00:21:20,467 --> 00:21:24,137
but I'm going to share everything
I see and hear on social media.

375
00:21:24,221 --> 00:21:28,266
I just want people back home
to see how great Japan is.

376
00:21:28,350 --> 00:21:31,103
Thank you very much. Enjoy yourself.

377
00:21:31,186 --> 00:21:33,146
Welcome to Japan.

378
00:21:35,315 --> 00:21:36,858
But what about myself?

379
00:21:38,151 --> 00:21:39,444
Paying attention

380
00:21:39,528 --> 00:21:42,114
to other people's belongings here,

381
00:21:42,197 --> 00:21:44,241
while grinding my nerves down…

382
00:21:45,283 --> 00:21:47,077
I started to worry that I was losing

383
00:21:48,370 --> 00:21:50,872
important things,
like my own dreams and hopes.

384
00:21:56,878 --> 00:21:58,296
Hello. This is Seike.

385
00:21:59,714 --> 00:22:00,674
Yes.

386
00:22:03,844 --> 00:22:06,346
Matsuyama. The Counselor
is calling for you.

387
00:22:20,068 --> 00:22:24,990
Counselor Sugihara has decided
to suspend Matsuyama for the time being.

388
00:22:25,073 --> 00:22:27,868
-Really?
-Because you two made a fuss out of it.

389
00:22:27,951 --> 00:22:29,202
Hold on now.

390
00:22:29,286 --> 00:22:31,872
The fact that he was released
is thanks to us.

391
00:22:31,955 --> 00:22:34,833
Yes. We're having a hard time
dealing with Nishida ourselves.

392
00:22:34,916 --> 00:22:35,792
That's right.

393
00:22:35,876 --> 00:22:38,461
He hasn't had any remarkable
results lately, so he's getting impatient.

394
00:22:38,545 --> 00:22:42,174
Then he came into our territory
to get a smuggling and murder case.

395
00:22:42,257 --> 00:22:43,884
He's a real piece of work.

396
00:22:43,967 --> 00:22:47,137
That 43-year-old man makes my blood boil.

397
00:22:47,220 --> 00:22:49,890
Is it fine to speak so freely
about your colleague's personal matters?

398
00:22:49,973 --> 00:22:51,725
This isn't personal information.

399
00:22:53,226 --> 00:22:54,060
It's badmouthing.

400
00:22:55,270 --> 00:22:57,189
-Neither is okay.
-Oh…

401
00:22:57,981 --> 00:22:58,940
Um…

402
00:23:01,401 --> 00:23:03,820
May I ask one thing?

403
00:23:05,655 --> 00:23:08,283
What did Amita bring in?

404
00:23:09,284 --> 00:23:12,037
Security cameras at the hotel
where the victim checked in

405
00:23:12,120 --> 00:23:14,456
showed her leaving the hotel

406
00:23:14,539 --> 00:23:16,541
holding a paper shopping bag.

407
00:23:17,125 --> 00:23:22,589
However, that paper bag wasn't at the park
so we think the perpetrator took it.

408
00:23:23,131 --> 00:23:26,927
This is a photo of her suitcase.

409
00:23:33,433 --> 00:23:36,102
It looks as though something
has been removed entirely.

410
00:23:36,186 --> 00:23:38,980
She probably took whatever
was stored there with her.

411
00:23:40,440 --> 00:23:43,944
Is this suitcase size medium or large?

412
00:23:47,447 --> 00:23:49,366
Roughly about this big, I suppose.

413
00:23:49,449 --> 00:23:51,201
In that case, it's a medium.

414
00:23:51,284 --> 00:23:53,620
An M-size suitcase is generally

415
00:23:53,703 --> 00:23:56,790
66 cm tall, 44 cm wide,

416
00:23:56,873 --> 00:23:58,875
and 27 cm deep.

417
00:23:58,959 --> 00:24:01,336
Estimating the blank space
from those dimensions,

418
00:24:01,419 --> 00:24:06,216
it's about 19 cm tall, 14 cm wide,
and 10 cm deep.

419
00:24:07,092 --> 00:24:07,926
Something like this.

420
00:24:08,009 --> 00:24:09,511
What is that?

421
00:24:09,594 --> 00:24:11,429
I wonder. Some kind of box?

422
00:24:11,513 --> 00:24:14,516
Some kind of book, perhaps?
Like a dictionary.

423
00:24:14,599 --> 00:24:17,560
Who brings a paper dictionary
on a trip nowadays?

424
00:24:18,353 --> 00:24:22,357
If it were a hardcover book,
it would be 20 cm tall and 15 cm wide.

425
00:24:22,440 --> 00:24:25,777
It's close, but book sizes
vary by country.

426
00:24:26,361 --> 00:24:28,363
Or perhaps…

427
00:24:35,787 --> 00:24:37,580
-A DVD?
-Yes.

428
00:24:38,164 --> 00:24:41,251
DVD cases are a universal size.

429
00:24:41,334 --> 00:24:44,504
Nineteen cm tall and 13 cm wide.

430
00:24:44,587 --> 00:24:48,383
A DVD box set fits perfectly into
the square space of Amita's suitcase.

431
00:24:48,466 --> 00:24:50,927
Do you remember if there was
something like that in the suitcase?

432
00:24:53,096 --> 00:24:56,182
Now that you mention it, a DVD set…

433
00:24:56,266 --> 00:24:57,434
It was there, right?

434
00:24:58,143 --> 00:24:59,686
I only vaguely remember,

435
00:25:00,270 --> 00:25:04,024
but it looked like a romance, with a man
and a woman staring at each other.

436
00:25:04,107 --> 00:25:05,942
A man and a woman staring at each other…

437
00:25:06,651 --> 00:25:10,947
But after that, my focus
was taken up by her necklace.

438
00:25:11,031 --> 00:25:12,073
Ah, really…

439
00:25:12,657 --> 00:25:14,951
The soil in that necklace
really caught your eye, huh?

440
00:25:15,785 --> 00:25:20,373
I noticed it because I'd confiscated
the same necklace in the past. I think…

441
00:25:20,457 --> 00:25:22,083
The same necklace?

442
00:25:22,625 --> 00:25:23,501
Yes.

443
00:25:24,711 --> 00:25:29,007
The same customs officer
confiscated the same necklace.

444
00:25:29,090 --> 00:25:31,843
Is that just a coincidence?

445
00:25:38,183 --> 00:25:41,853
This is a record of the necklace
Matsuyama previously confiscated.

446
00:25:41,936 --> 00:25:43,229
Utsugi, nice play!

447
00:25:43,313 --> 00:25:46,066
This is the necklace
confiscated from Amita.

448
00:25:46,608 --> 00:25:47,942
Yes, they are identical.

449
00:25:48,443 --> 00:25:51,279
Hana Chaplan. She was also from Chatwan.

450
00:25:51,363 --> 00:25:53,823
What is she doing now?

451
00:25:54,616 --> 00:25:55,867
What do you mean?

452
00:25:55,950 --> 00:25:57,577
Well, do you think

453
00:25:57,660 --> 00:26:00,372
the same thing that happened to Amita
could have happened to her?

454
00:26:01,748 --> 00:26:03,208
I'll check the entry and exit records.

455
00:26:05,668 --> 00:26:08,671
I feel like I've seen
this necklace somewhere…

456
00:26:13,802 --> 00:26:14,844
Oh my.

457
00:26:17,972 --> 00:26:23,395
This is a DVD of a romance drama that
enjoyed immense popularity in Chatwan.

458
00:26:23,478 --> 00:26:26,356
It's a story where a pilot
injured in an accident

459
00:26:26,439 --> 00:26:28,358
and a flight attendant engaged

460
00:26:28,441 --> 00:26:30,318
to a wealthy tycoon reunite
on a hill of memories

461
00:26:30,402 --> 00:26:32,612
at the end of the drama
and reclaim their love.

462
00:26:32,695 --> 00:26:35,240
So cliché. But I love that kind of stuff.

463
00:26:35,323 --> 00:26:36,366
Huh?

464
00:26:36,449 --> 00:26:40,161
You didn't know Korean idols,
but you're well-versed in Chatwan dramas?

465
00:26:40,245 --> 00:26:43,164
Yes. I learned from the Korean idols case,
so I studied up.

466
00:26:43,248 --> 00:26:45,375
Is that drama connected
to the necklace in some way?

467
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:47,043
Yes.

468
00:26:48,128 --> 00:26:52,257
This necklace is a bonus item
that comes with purchasing the DVD set.

469
00:26:52,340 --> 00:26:54,384
-A bonus item?
-Yes.

470
00:26:54,467 --> 00:26:57,720
And the soil inside this bottle

471
00:26:58,388 --> 00:27:00,723
is from this hill of memories.

472
00:27:02,642 --> 00:27:03,852
I found her.

473
00:27:03,935 --> 00:27:06,521
Hana Chaplan, 25 years old.
She's still in the country.

474
00:27:11,025 --> 00:27:14,654
Hana Chaplan was a college student
who came to Japan as a monitor

475
00:27:14,737 --> 00:27:16,698
to post about her stay
in Japan on social media.

476
00:27:16,781 --> 00:27:21,286
It seems she had all
travel expenses to Japan paid for.

477
00:27:21,369 --> 00:27:23,746
However, there was a condition.

478
00:27:24,330 --> 00:27:25,373
A condition?

479
00:27:30,211 --> 00:27:32,839
When you arrive in Japan, I want you
to hand this to a friend of mine.

480
00:27:33,882 --> 00:27:35,758
Is there something wrong with that?

481
00:27:35,842 --> 00:27:38,887
Of course not.
You know this drama too, right?

482
00:27:38,970 --> 00:27:40,930
My friend wants to watch it.

483
00:27:42,182 --> 00:27:45,226
This is a bonus item you get
when you buy the set.

484
00:27:45,310 --> 00:27:47,312
-Put it on.
-Thank you.

485
00:27:47,395 --> 00:27:52,025
It would be troublesome if those DVDs
got confiscated at customs by mistake,

486
00:27:52,108 --> 00:27:53,943
so make sure to go through
inspection with that man.

487
00:27:54,652 --> 00:27:58,072
Amita likely received
the same instruction.

488
00:27:58,156 --> 00:27:59,908
What is in that DVD?

489
00:27:59,991 --> 00:28:01,701
I thought maybe it was something

490
00:28:01,784 --> 00:28:05,538
available only over there, traded
at high prices as a collector's item.

491
00:28:05,622 --> 00:28:08,541
It was not something
with that kind of value.

492
00:28:08,625 --> 00:28:09,542
I see.

493
00:28:11,252 --> 00:28:13,838
So you all looked into this.

494
00:28:13,922 --> 00:28:16,424
Yes. As you can see,
we haven't neglected our duties.

495
00:28:18,051 --> 00:28:19,511
It's just frustrating, isn't it?

496
00:28:19,594 --> 00:28:23,723
We can lift Matsuyama's
suspension now, right?

497
00:28:26,351 --> 00:28:28,978
He submitted his resignation.

498
00:28:33,691 --> 00:28:36,861
He submitted his resignation.

499
00:28:37,445 --> 00:28:41,699
He said that as a customs officer
suspected of aiding in smuggling,

500
00:28:41,783 --> 00:28:44,661
he can't continue doing the job.

501
00:28:47,247 --> 00:28:48,289
Matsuyama

502
00:28:49,040 --> 00:28:51,209
hasn't done anything wrong, though.

503
00:28:52,377 --> 00:28:53,503
Yes.

504
00:28:53,586 --> 00:28:58,591
However, Amita and Hana were instructed
to go through Matsuyama's booth

505
00:28:58,675 --> 00:29:00,593
and were given his photo.

506
00:29:01,719 --> 00:29:04,264
Unless the reason for that becomes clear,

507
00:29:04,347 --> 00:29:06,182
the suspicion surrounding him
won't be cleared.

508
00:29:06,266 --> 00:29:08,059
In that case, we should
find that out as well.

509
00:29:15,775 --> 00:29:19,153
This is the photo of Matsuyama
that Hana and Amita received.

510
00:29:19,237 --> 00:29:20,738
That's our booth.

511
00:29:20,822 --> 00:29:22,073
Photography is prohibited there.

512
00:29:22,156 --> 00:29:23,992
-They must have taken it secretly.
-Yes.

513
00:29:24,075 --> 00:29:26,744
It's during shift hours.
He's standing there blankly.

514
00:29:26,828 --> 00:29:27,787
True.

515
00:29:27,871 --> 00:29:31,207
Judging from the angle,
it was taken from in front of the exit.

516
00:29:32,375 --> 00:29:36,129
If an arriving passenger is in the photo,
we might be able to identify the flight.

517
00:29:36,671 --> 00:29:38,590
Is there any benefit
to knowing the flight?

518
00:29:38,673 --> 00:29:40,425
We'll know what day this photo was taken.

519
00:29:40,508 --> 00:29:42,343
I see. If we know the date and time,

520
00:29:42,427 --> 00:29:44,470
we can identify the photographer
using CCTV.

521
00:29:45,638 --> 00:29:46,764
Um…

522
00:29:49,183 --> 00:29:50,810
What is this?

523
00:29:52,812 --> 00:29:53,771
Fabric?

524
00:29:55,106 --> 00:29:56,024
Clothing?

525
00:29:58,067 --> 00:30:01,029
Isn't this a hat?

526
00:30:01,112 --> 00:30:04,449
At this height, a child?

527
00:30:04,991 --> 00:30:06,117
An elementary school student.

528
00:30:06,200 --> 00:30:09,412
An elementary school student
with a white hat…

529
00:30:15,209 --> 00:30:16,628
-The field trip!
-The field trip!

530
00:30:17,211 --> 00:30:19,881
The students from Akikasho Elementary
came on a field trip

531
00:30:19,964 --> 00:30:23,927
on June 29th, from 1:00 p.m. to 1:30 p.m.

532
00:30:28,556 --> 00:30:29,724
It's this man.

533
00:30:30,433 --> 00:30:31,809
Hold on, hold on.

534
00:30:32,393 --> 00:30:35,313
It's not all good, you know.

535
00:30:35,897 --> 00:30:38,107
She received instructions

536
00:30:38,191 --> 00:30:40,985
and did something dangerous.

537
00:30:46,282 --> 00:30:47,700
Sorry to bother you.

538
00:30:47,784 --> 00:30:49,202
We're the police.

539
00:30:50,328 --> 00:30:53,122
PREPARING

540
00:30:53,206 --> 00:30:55,458
You took this photo, didn't you?

541
00:30:55,541 --> 00:30:59,337
Your boss had a villa in Chatwan, right?

542
00:30:59,420 --> 00:31:01,005
What were you doing,
using that villa as a base?

543
00:31:01,089 --> 00:31:02,966
I don't know anything.
I'm not a gang member.

544
00:31:03,049 --> 00:31:05,802
You were waiting in a black car
for the boss to return, weren't you?

545
00:31:05,885 --> 00:31:07,845
You're basically a member.

546
00:31:09,430 --> 00:31:12,809
The woman who had this photo
on her smartphone was murdered.

547
00:31:12,892 --> 00:31:15,561
You're already involved in this.

548
00:31:15,645 --> 00:31:18,231
-I don't know anything about a murder!
-Then what do you know?

549
00:31:18,314 --> 00:31:19,524
-Sit down. Come on.
-No,

550
00:31:19,607 --> 00:31:22,068
-You took the photo!
-I don't know anything!

551
00:31:22,151 --> 00:31:22,986
No,

552
00:31:23,069 --> 00:31:24,821
-I didn't do anything…
-What are you doing here?

553
00:31:24,904 --> 00:31:26,030
May I have a moment?

554
00:31:26,864 --> 00:31:28,241
Sit tight.

555
00:31:28,950 --> 00:31:30,118
What is it?

556
00:31:30,201 --> 00:31:33,413
Um, do you always do things like this?

557
00:31:33,496 --> 00:31:36,165
Well, yes. Don't like it?

558
00:31:36,249 --> 00:31:38,251
We're doing this for all your sakes.

559
00:31:38,334 --> 00:31:40,420
-Well, that's enough then.
-What?

560
00:31:54,892 --> 00:31:55,935
What are you doing?

561
00:31:56,519 --> 00:31:59,063
-I'm looking at your eyes.
-My eyes?

562
00:32:03,443 --> 00:32:04,736
Because of my job,

563
00:32:05,528 --> 00:32:08,614
I look at the eyes of people
from many different countries.

564
00:32:10,158 --> 00:32:14,746
Among them, very rarely,
there are people with eyes like yours.

565
00:32:16,789 --> 00:32:18,124
What kind of eyes?

566
00:32:18,708 --> 00:32:21,044
Eyes wavering between good and evil.

567
00:32:23,379 --> 00:32:25,256
The eyes of someone standing
on the edge of a cliff.

568
00:32:29,427 --> 00:32:31,929
Because of the photo you took,

569
00:32:33,222 --> 00:32:34,390
a woman lost her life,

570
00:32:36,392 --> 00:32:38,603
and a man was thrown off
the tracks of his life.

571
00:32:39,645 --> 00:32:42,565
You can't get back her life.
That mistake won't go away.

572
00:32:43,066 --> 00:32:46,736
But right now, it's still possible
to save a man's life.

573
00:32:50,114 --> 00:32:51,532
The only one who can do that

574
00:32:52,658 --> 00:32:53,826
is you.

575
00:33:01,876 --> 00:33:03,044
All right,

576
00:33:03,753 --> 00:33:04,712
Detective.

577
00:33:05,922 --> 00:33:08,091
-Okay.
-Amazing…

578
00:33:09,092 --> 00:33:10,218
Here you go.

579
00:33:11,969 --> 00:33:13,805
Sorry it's not katsudon.

580
00:33:14,847 --> 00:33:16,015
Thank you.

581
00:33:17,141 --> 00:33:19,477
He's not a detective, though.

582
00:33:19,560 --> 00:33:21,771
It seems that man

583
00:33:22,688 --> 00:33:26,692
looked into the customs officers
at Gate 24

584
00:33:26,776 --> 00:33:28,903
for the smuggling.

585
00:33:30,154 --> 00:33:32,156
He looked into the customs officers?

586
00:33:32,240 --> 00:33:33,991
Not many flights come from Chatwan,

587
00:33:34,075 --> 00:33:37,245
so they always enter through that gate.

588
00:33:38,246 --> 00:33:41,290
The officers gathered at a newly built,
isolated gate like that

589
00:33:42,125 --> 00:33:45,670
are just a ragtag group,
and inspections are lax.

590
00:33:45,753 --> 00:33:49,507
I was instructed to pick the one who
seemed especially lax and send a photo.

591
00:33:49,590 --> 00:33:51,551
And the one chosen

592
00:33:51,634 --> 00:33:54,387
was Matsuyama, who was the youngest
and seemed the most good-natured.

593
00:33:55,429 --> 00:33:57,348
He wasn't an accomplice.

594
00:33:57,431 --> 00:33:58,683
He was a victim.

595
00:33:59,183 --> 00:34:01,519
A ragtag group with lax inspections.

596
00:34:02,311 --> 00:34:04,397
They really were taking us for fools, huh.

597
00:34:06,232 --> 00:34:10,695
I reported this to Detective Nishida
to clear his suspicion.

598
00:34:11,487 --> 00:34:13,281
Then a proposal came from their side.

599
00:34:14,949 --> 00:34:17,368
We obtained information that a woman

600
00:34:17,451 --> 00:34:20,955
carrying that DVD
is on the next flight from Chatwan.

601
00:34:21,747 --> 00:34:22,790
So,

602
00:34:22,874 --> 00:34:25,418
we want you to let that woman
enter the country.

603
00:34:26,627 --> 00:34:27,962
Why me?

604
00:34:28,045 --> 00:34:32,091
She has been instructed
to undergo inspection by you.

605
00:34:32,842 --> 00:34:34,886
Just like with Amita.

606
00:34:35,386 --> 00:34:38,806
The one who killed her is almost certainly
the person receiving the DVD.

607
00:34:38,890 --> 00:34:40,933
We'll have the woman
guide us to that person.

608
00:34:42,143 --> 00:34:44,604
You're telling me to send
a woman to a murderer?

609
00:34:44,687 --> 00:34:47,231
We will do everything possible
to ensure her safety.

610
00:34:47,940 --> 00:34:50,484
We want to catch the killer
no matter what.

611
00:34:50,568 --> 00:34:52,862
You feel the same, don't you?

612
00:34:55,489 --> 00:34:57,241
‎GATE 24 - SECONDARY ROOMGATE 24
‎SECONDARY ROOM

613
00:35:27,855 --> 00:35:29,732
‎GATE 24 - IN FRONT OF BOOTH A &amp; B

614
00:35:31,776 --> 00:35:33,486
Mori, what are you doing?

615
00:35:33,569 --> 00:35:36,280
-I'm investigating.
-Investigating what?

616
00:35:36,822 --> 00:35:38,157
It's been bothering me.

617
00:35:38,741 --> 00:35:42,954
Why is the smuggling group trying to bring
in the same DVD over and over again?

618
00:35:46,415 --> 00:35:50,169
I don't want to leave
questions unanswered.

619
00:36:10,439 --> 00:36:11,274
She's here.

620
00:36:25,037 --> 00:36:26,622
Oh my…

621
00:36:28,874 --> 00:36:31,460
-Your passport, please.
-Here you go.

622
00:36:38,718 --> 00:36:40,803
-Please proceed to baggage check.
-Okay.

623
00:36:41,804 --> 00:36:43,764
May I see inside?

624
00:36:47,435 --> 00:36:48,519
Here.

625
00:37:02,074 --> 00:37:03,034
What is this?

626
00:37:04,076 --> 00:37:07,705
It's a DVD set.
A famous drama from my country.

627
00:37:09,415 --> 00:37:11,751
Really? Understood.

628
00:37:19,258 --> 00:37:21,761
-I will inspect the inside of this again.
-Okay.

629
00:37:22,386 --> 00:37:23,346
What are you doing?

630
00:37:23,429 --> 00:37:26,766
-This DVD might contain steganography.
-What?

631
00:37:26,849 --> 00:37:29,352
It's an information-hiding method
where other data

632
00:37:29,435 --> 00:37:30,936
is embedded inside recorded data.

633
00:37:37,860 --> 00:37:40,780
This DVD has been altered…

634
00:37:42,823 --> 00:37:44,367
and the light reflection is unusual.

635
00:37:45,076 --> 00:37:46,243
Hey.

636
00:37:46,327 --> 00:37:47,870
What are you doing?

637
00:37:48,746 --> 00:37:49,955
‎This one too.

638
00:37:50,039 --> 00:37:51,624
What's going on?

639
00:37:51,707 --> 00:37:53,459
This DVD has other information

640
00:37:53,542 --> 00:37:55,461
-hidden on it.
-Mori, that's enough.

641
00:38:01,384 --> 00:38:03,052
There's no problem. Go ahead.

642
00:38:03,135 --> 00:38:04,303
That way, please.

643
00:38:04,929 --> 00:38:05,763
‎Thank you.

644
00:38:09,725 --> 00:38:10,976
Matsuyama.

645
00:38:12,144 --> 00:38:13,145
Are you okay with this?

646
00:38:15,356 --> 00:38:18,526
What is our job?

647
00:38:21,237 --> 00:38:22,488
Our

648
00:38:22,571 --> 00:38:23,948
job?

649
00:38:39,797 --> 00:38:41,757
You cannot bring those DVDs in!

650
00:38:42,299 --> 00:38:44,009
I'm confiscating them.

651
00:38:45,010 --> 00:38:46,846
What is he doing!?

652
00:38:48,055 --> 00:38:49,557
What? Why?

653
00:38:50,141 --> 00:38:54,895
It has information that is prohibited
from being taken out of your country.

654
00:38:55,479 --> 00:38:58,357
What are you talking about?
That's impossible.

655
00:38:58,441 --> 00:39:00,693
You were asked to hand this DVD

656
00:39:00,776 --> 00:39:03,320
over to a certain person.

657
00:39:04,238 --> 00:39:05,698
How do you know about that?

658
00:39:07,408 --> 00:39:11,203
There was a woman who came
from Chatwan just like you.

659
00:39:12,246 --> 00:39:13,164
But

660
00:39:13,914 --> 00:39:15,332
she was killed.

661
00:39:16,709 --> 00:39:19,253
I don't want the same thing
to happen to you.

662
00:39:28,262 --> 00:39:31,682
You ruined the plan.
What were you thinking!?

663
00:39:33,767 --> 00:39:34,852
What's with that look?

664
00:39:35,811 --> 00:39:38,189
Mori was just doing her job.

665
00:39:38,272 --> 00:39:39,356
What did you say?

666
00:39:41,400 --> 00:39:44,945
Finding things that must not
be brought in,

667
00:39:45,029 --> 00:39:47,114
that's our job in Customs.

668
00:39:47,823 --> 00:39:49,033
Your results have nothing to do with it.

669
00:39:49,116 --> 00:39:50,868
Don't be so naive!

670
00:39:51,452 --> 00:39:53,746
That's why organized crime
takes advantage of you!

671
00:40:00,628 --> 00:40:01,670
Matsuyama.

672
00:40:04,215 --> 00:40:05,174
Welcome

673
00:40:05,883 --> 00:40:06,759
to Japan.

674
00:40:08,427 --> 00:40:09,345
What?

675
00:40:09,428 --> 00:40:11,180
Welcome to Japan.

676
00:40:12,556 --> 00:40:13,849
That's what I said

677
00:40:15,100 --> 00:40:17,144
when I welcomed Amita into this country.

678
00:40:18,479 --> 00:40:19,522
But

679
00:40:20,606 --> 00:40:22,024
right after that…

680
00:40:23,692 --> 00:40:26,820
her life was taken
by someone from this country.

681
00:40:30,366 --> 00:40:31,575
Do you have

682
00:40:32,618 --> 00:40:36,080
any idea how deeply regrettable that is?

683
00:40:42,545 --> 00:40:44,964
Don't think you'll get off easy for this.

684
00:40:47,675 --> 00:40:49,843
Are you going to fire me
using your authority?

685
00:40:50,511 --> 00:40:53,305
I've already submitted my resignation.

686
00:40:54,098 --> 00:40:55,349
Do as you like.

687
00:41:10,281 --> 00:41:13,617
This morning, a report came in
from the Metropolitan Police Department.

688
00:41:14,243 --> 00:41:16,495
The person who received
the DVDs was arrested

689
00:41:17,246 --> 00:41:19,582
and has reportedly confessed
to Amita's murder.

690
00:41:21,875 --> 00:41:23,335
Why did he…

691
00:41:23,877 --> 00:41:29,341
The man invited Amita, who brought
the DVDs, for drinks, but she declined.

692
00:41:30,175 --> 00:41:32,136
Enraged, he shoved her,

693
00:41:32,219 --> 00:41:33,929
and she fell and struck her head.

694
00:41:34,847 --> 00:41:36,056
Over something like that…

695
00:41:37,349 --> 00:41:39,768
Triggered by the man's statement,

696
00:41:39,852 --> 00:41:43,147
the crime group that planned to bring in
the classified info was also arrested.

697
00:41:44,857 --> 00:41:45,691
I see.

698
00:41:46,650 --> 00:41:47,484
Now then…

699
00:41:51,614 --> 00:41:52,656
…what do we do with this?

700
00:41:53,907 --> 00:41:55,576
NOTICE OF RESIGNATION

701
00:42:00,414 --> 00:42:02,333
On a Chatwan news site,

702
00:42:02,416 --> 00:42:04,918
there was an article about a Japanese
researcher at a medical equipment firm

703
00:42:05,002 --> 00:42:08,380
being arrested for leaking
classified information.

704
00:42:08,464 --> 00:42:10,549
The researcher sold classified information

705
00:42:10,633 --> 00:42:14,053
to a Japanese organized crime group
to cover debts.

706
00:42:14,136 --> 00:42:17,556
And they tried to record that
onto a DVD and bring it in.

707
00:42:17,640 --> 00:42:20,017
But why go through
the trouble of using a DVD?

708
00:42:20,100 --> 00:42:22,811
Customs checks
on USB flash drives are strict,

709
00:42:22,895 --> 00:42:25,939
which is why I think they recorded it
on a DVD, an older storage medium.

710
00:42:31,111 --> 00:42:32,446
Um, everyone--

711
00:42:32,529 --> 00:42:36,408
-It'll be hard to replace you.
-True.

712
00:42:36,492 --> 00:42:38,160
-Chief, actually--
-We

713
00:42:38,243 --> 00:42:41,497
all apologize. We were
wrong to suspect you.

714
00:42:42,706 --> 00:42:45,084
Let me say one last thing.

715
00:42:46,168 --> 00:42:47,920
We went through a lot together.

716
00:42:48,003 --> 00:42:50,839
Looking back, you were
an excellent customs officer.

717
00:42:51,465 --> 00:42:52,883
-Thank you for everything.
-No, um--

718
00:42:52,966 --> 00:42:56,929
Sorry for thinking you have such a naive
baby face, you can't handle this job.

719
00:42:57,012 --> 00:42:59,556
-Right?
-No, that's not what I--

720
00:42:59,640 --> 00:43:01,392
Everyone, please listen. I--

721
00:43:01,475 --> 00:43:03,727
You decided not to quit, didn't you?

722
00:43:06,188 --> 00:43:09,358
Counselor Sugihara called a moment ago.

723
00:43:09,441 --> 00:43:13,904
After receiving this much care,
quitting isn't an option, is it?

724
00:43:17,783 --> 00:43:18,826
Here.

725
00:43:19,952 --> 00:43:21,078
What is this?

726
00:43:21,745 --> 00:43:22,788
Classified information.

727
00:43:33,006 --> 00:43:34,633
‎TO THE MISTER

728
00:43:40,180 --> 00:43:43,809
Mister, sorry for calling you lame
the other day.

729
00:43:44,727 --> 00:43:48,397
Thank you for working hard to protect us.

730
00:43:49,440 --> 00:43:52,526
-You got this!
-You got this!

731
00:43:52,609 --> 00:43:56,113
-You got this!
-You got this!

732
00:44:02,369 --> 00:44:04,830
I thought they were just annoying kids…

733
00:44:06,290 --> 00:44:07,791
They were really paying attention

734
00:44:07,875 --> 00:44:09,668
to our work, huh?

735
00:44:12,129 --> 00:44:13,797
Our job is opening people's luggage,

736
00:44:14,631 --> 00:44:16,091
taking away bad stuff,

737
00:44:17,259 --> 00:44:19,386
with people angry at you.

738
00:44:20,053 --> 00:44:21,054
But

739
00:44:22,389 --> 00:44:24,349
if that protects someone…

740
00:44:26,643 --> 00:44:28,479
it's not a bad job, right?

741
00:44:38,280 --> 00:44:39,615
Welcome back.

742
00:44:44,828 --> 00:44:48,123
‎Hundrends of millions of yen worth
‎of drugs are about to be carried in.

743
00:44:48,207 --> 00:44:51,168
‎We have to inspect the urn…

744
00:44:51,251 --> 00:44:52,628
‎What if we don't find anything?

745
00:44:52,711 --> 00:44:54,338
‎Women don't lie.

746
00:44:54,421 --> 00:44:56,006
‎What else could you be suspecting me of?

747
00:44:56,089 --> 00:44:58,008
‎We sincerely apologize to you.

748
00:44:58,091 --> 00:44:59,134
‎This is going to be a big problem.

749
00:44:59,218 --> 00:45:00,093
Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman

